# Round cardtile (T), the landing A/B: the grouped shadow as (card expert, row tile, 8-column tile) items
# against today's per-slot walk, one binary, BLOOMERY_CARD_EXPERTS=tile against =expert. Flow model
# (tools/flow, round flowb1): on the prose prompt the B1 shadow is 45.3 ms a layer-batch measured (per slot
# 45.6 [derived] with the prompt's routing) against a 36.4 ms union, and after T 17.8 [15.5-19.9] [derived],
# under the union on every layer; the wall becomes route window + union + prologue. B1+T 221.5 [213.4-228.3]
# over B1 183.8 at the lcg clock, 175.8 at the measured card-bound clock (171.6 measured, 09-26#b1-pp-ab).
# lcg moves 0 at both P (its shadow is already under the union), so the lcg arm is not the term.
kind: ab
question: does cardtile take the grouped shadow off the prose prompt's P = 512 path, as the flow
  model's route + union wall says?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 512, prose prompt (corpus-prose.ids, the first 512), hot list 384, A6000, plan
  (a), CED on - (tile - expert) / expert, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +17.1..+25.2
rounds: 2
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, two binaries' per-round pp ratios, one run's SD about 0.55
  and 1.1 %; the larger
condition: the cardtile binary, both arms in one lease through its lever, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_HOT_LIST=/root/bloomery-data/router/hotlist-384.txt BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1
  BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/cardtile-pp.card' just depth-gpu-ds41 prose:512
  prose:512@BLOOMERY_CARD_EXPERTS=expert prose:4096 prose:4096@BLOOMERY_CARD_EXPERTS=expert (the prose
  arm, fixup7b), the order rotated each round, card_in, card_out and wait printed per arm; no row
  carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]. The P = 4096 rows are read against the band +15.8..+22.8, and the
  witness clocks (SM clock, the power-slowdown counter's post - pre) are read beside card_out for the
  card-bound clock hypothesis
decide-in: keep T and build prefillgroup (G): after T the prose P = 4096 card (40 ms a layer-batch)
  and host (42) are balanced and only the wrap overlaps them
decide-below: read card_in: above ~22 ms the tile items run below e 0.45 (registers, occupancy) -
  ptxas -v and ncu the GT kernel and split gate and up before G; at or under 20 ms the route kept the
  card-bound clock - sample the SM clock through one prompt
decide-above: the route ran faster than the card-bound clock allows (card duty fell to ~0.66): write
  the tile arm's card_out into clk_cardbound's duty curve, then G
